errors.wf:1:9: error: inherit paths are not quoted
  |
1 | inherit "/std/room"
  |         ^^^^^^^^^^^
  = help: write `inherit /std/room`
errors.wf:4:19: error: expected an expression, found `=`
  |
4 | var broken: int = = 2
  |                   ^
errors.wf:8:5: error: expected an expression, found `let`
  |
8 |     let y = @
  |     ^^^
errors.wf:8:13: error: unexpected character `@`
  |
8 |     let y = @
  |             ^
errors.wf:10:16: error: expected `{`, found `return`
   |
10 |     while true return
   |                ^^^^^^
errors.wf:11:11: error: expected end of statement, found integer `2`
   |
11 |     x = 1 2
   |           ^
   = help: put each statement on its own line or separate them with `;`
errors.wf:12:5: error: cannot assign to this expression
   |
12 |     1 + 2 = 3
   |     ^^^^^
   = help: assign to a variable (`x = …`) or an element (`a[i] = …`)
errors.wf:13:17: error: empty `{}` in interpolated string
   |
13 |     let s = $"a {  } b"
   |                 ^^^^
errors.wf:16:1: error: `import` is not supported in the Phase 0 Weft subset
   |
16 | import /x/y
   | ^^^^^^
   = help: use `inherit` for code reuse in Phase 0
errors.wf:19:18: error: comparison operators cannot be chained
   |
19 |     return a < b < c
   |                  ^
   = help: combine comparisons with `and`: `a < b and b < c`
